{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And he sent Judah before him to Joseph.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he sent Judah before him to prepare a house for him in Goshen, because he was the mightiest and most zealous of the brothers. And our Sages, of blessed memory, scrutinized the word להורות ('to instruct' / 'to prepare') and said: to establish for him a house of study, where he would give instruction there, so that the tribes would be engaged in Torah. You can know that this is so, for when Joseph parted from his father they were engaged in Torah in the passage of the broken-necked heifer (עגלה ערופה); when he saw the wagons he remembered that in the passage of the broken-necked heifer he had parted from him, and then he believed, and this is what is written (Genesis 45:27): ״וירא את העגלות״ — 'and he saw the wagons,' etc., and it is written (ibid.): ״ותחי רוח יעקב״ — 'and the spirit of Jacob revived.'" "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> ״ואת יהודה שלח לפניו״ — Yesterday an ox and a lion were goring each other, and now he goes to him on an errand; this is what Scripture said (Isaiah 65): ״זאב וטלה ירעו כאחד ואריה כבקר יאכל תבן״ — 'The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like cattle.' Wolf — this is Benjamin, as it is said: ״בנימן זאב יטרף״; and lamb — these are the tribes, as it is said (Jeremiah 50): ״שה פזורה ישראל״. 'Shall feed together' — that Benjamin went down with them, for Jacob had said: ״לא ירד בני עמכם״; when the hour arrived and he went down with them, they cushioned him and guarded him. 'And the lion' — this is Judah, as it is said (Genesis 49): ״גור אריה יהודה״. 'Like cattle shall eat straw' — this is Joseph, as it is said (Deuteronomy 33): ״בכור שורו הדר לו״. Thus they were eating together, as it is said (Genesis 43): ״וישבו לפניו הבכור כבכורתו״; hence you may say: ״ואת יהודה שלח לפניו אל יוסף״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:53.643574029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}